// The node kinds. Every one is a zero-action named function, so a bare literal
// kind never appears at a call site and this file is the only place the numbers
// live.
//
// Each is `(import ast_kbase) + n`, not a plain literal: `id` rejects two functions whose
// bodies match up to renaming, and a zero-action function returning a bare
// integer is distinguished by nothing but that integer -- so a literal 12 here
// would collide with a literal 12 in any other module's constant. Naming the base
// puts a called function into every fingerprint, and puts the family's origin in
// one place.
//
// The order matters exactly once: ast_kn holds the printable name of each kind at
// index (kind - (import ast_kbase)), filled from one space-separated string in ast_kinit.
//
// Field convention, obeyed by every kind so that the dumper needs no per-kind
// knowledge: ast_a, ast_b and ast_c are always node ids (0 = absent), ast_kids is
// always a list of node ids, and the only kind that stores a plain integer is
// `num` (a = value, b = fractional digits still owed to a slot).

ast_k_nil() {
  int v = (import ast_kbase) + 0;
} return int v;

ast_k_file() {
  int v = (import ast_kbase) + 1;
} return int v;
